Atlasmith itself bundles no third-party source code. Its required dependencies
(trimesh, numpy, Pillow, xatlas) and its optional "[ml]" dependencies are
fetched from PyPI by the package manager at install time; Atlasmith neither
vendors nor redistributes them.


Optional "[ml]" extra
---------------------

Installing the optional extra ("uv sync --extra ml" or
"pip install atlasmith[ml]") pulls in the following direct dependencies:

  * torch (PyTorch) -- composite license expression, all permissive:
    Apache-2.0 AND Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception AND BSD-2-Clause AND
    BSD-3-Clause AND BSL-1.0 AND MIT
    https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/LICENSE

  * sam2 (Segment Anything Model 2, Meta Platforms, Inc.) -- Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2

  * moderngl -- MIT
    https://github.com/moderngl/moderngl

  * huggingface_hub -- Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/huggingface/huggingface_hub

No GPL, AGPL, or LGPL licensed package was found in the resolved dependency
set (Windows install set and Linux-only set of uv.lock were both checked).


Model weights (SAM2)
--------------------

Atlasmith does NOT ship, bundle, or redistribute any model weights.

When the SAM2 segmentation backend is used, the weights (default model id
"facebook/sam2.1-hiera-large") are downloaded at first run from the Hugging
Face Hub by the sam2 package. No authentication is required.

  * The SAM2 checkpoints are released by Meta Platforms, Inc. under the
    Apache License, Version 2.0 -- the same license as the SAM2 code.
  * SAM3 is published under a different, non-Apache "SAM License" and is
    deliberately NOT used by Atlasmith.

Users are responsible for complying with the license and the terms of use of
any model weights they download.


Third-party runtime components pulled in on Linux
-------------------------------------------------

On Linux, installing the "[ml]" extra additionally pulls in NVIDIA CUDA
runtime packages (nvidia-*, cuda-bindings, cuda-toolkit, ...) as transitive
dependencies of torch. Some of these are distributed under NVIDIA proprietary
licenses rather than an OSI-approved open source license. They are not
copyleft and are not redistributed by Atlasmith, but users should be aware of
them. One dependency (certifi) is licensed under MPL-2.0, a weak, per-file
copyleft license; Atlasmith does not modify it.

Details, primary sources, evidence grades and the reservations that apply to
these findings are recorded in:

    Docs/licenses/THIRD-PARTY-ML.md


